<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East: Palestinians plan first local elections in 20 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0229787872157a3748f25374d5a729d38da1197e3bff0fdaf25434f41bf731e1</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:29:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years--211e8e3008fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-palestinians-plan-first-local-elections-in-20-years" /><summary type="html">Oliver McTernan, Director and co-founder of Foward Thinking in London, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East: An art centre for children in occupied West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7202c85f1999ff36c11892e29d4b36e72f6464b00cd47a31ebde8595d88791a5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:10:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank--a778dd857aa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-an-art-centre-for-children-in-occupied-west-bank" /><summary type="html">To help children process their experiences of war, an art center has been established in the West Bank.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle-East: Iran proposes Hormuz plan, Donald Trump reportedly refuses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7e45f8146eccab2a9121682d08a527d776bf52d0cd7a531da357334f1c08f73</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:35:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses--0c236672cf1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-iran-proposes-hormuz-plan-donald-trump-reportedly-refuses" /><summary type="html">The United States had yet to publicly respond on Saturday after Iran offered a plan to reopen the strategic Strait of Hormuz, though reports indicated that President Donald Trump had rejected the proposal. The waterway key to the world's oil supply is central to the conflict between the US and Iran, which is at a stalemate after nearly seven months, though new mediation efforts took place this week.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis, Palestinians must 'reboot relations': Absence of diplomatic route means 'perpetual war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94d3f513c1cdddd4aa89fb5b18000f85212ed32e2d4ac3cd2d5abe92c5616799</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T07:50:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war--a967accb3eb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-palestinians-must-reboot-relations-absence-of-diplomatic-route-means-perpetual-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Yossi Mekelberg, Senior Consulting Fellow of the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House. Can Israel continue to define its future primarily through security and territorial control? Mekelberg challenges the notion that military operations, incursions and settlement expansion can constitute a sustainable political objective. He identifies a potential transition beyond the Netanyahu era as an opportunity to reconsider the relationship between Israeli and Palestinian societies. His central argument is that the continuation of war without a political endgame risks a state of perpetual conflict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump reportedly rejects Iran’s seven-day plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e1be49ecc8ff2bb304bc2ec4f4c6fee58d1900072a23fc4b6c962724b648299</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T02:06:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz--f4edda057a7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has reportedly rejected an Iranian plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz on Saturday. Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi presented the proposal to Trump’s envoy Steve Witkoff a day earlier on the sidelines of a UN gathering in New York. The plan stipulated that the important waterway would reopen seven days after an agreement was reached.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's president calls on his people to mobilise against Iran-backed Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9571710d00e8f93e0070de217dd2fdf53d4546242293518011e0a89797403222</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:41:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis--89065aa49aef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Riyadh-based President Rashid al-Alimi on Friday called on ‌his people to mobilise and join the armed ‌forces while offering a general amnesty to the Iran-backed Houthi rebels who have seized swaths of Yemen's Red Sea coast and imposed a naval blockade on Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Iran has dragged us into this conflict,' top Emirati diplomat Anwar Gargash says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e4d00860e9449d78452d6023a9b1afd9c68b9ab8d4ca559132a2a32340c54fa</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:04:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says--f3e23abd416a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24 on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Anwar Gargash, senior diplomatic adviser to the UAE president, said Iran "has dragged us into this conflict", after the UAE was "the target of 3,300 missiles and drones" fired by Iran. After US President Donald Trump said he could either negotiate with or "obliterate" Iran, Gargash warned that the "current situation of no war, no peace is not sustainable".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Macron says ‘military resources’ to be sent to Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dc2cb04165ac4bef2c90d4a0c327f55de8e2264a097cbeb01f1f498c937baff</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:04:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/macron-says-military-resources-to-be-sent-to-saudi-arabia--23b178d3533f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/macron-says-military-resources-to-be-sent-to-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Speaking to broadcasters TF1 and France 2, French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday announced that “military resources” will be sent to protect the Yanbu oil site in Saudi Arabia, integral to maintaining the kingdom’s fuel exports and increasingly threatened by Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthi rebels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tehran offers US seven-day plan to open Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96a750a0676d4b37b053abbba2879742d0417e11b2d553660ff348aceed1d64b</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:52:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war--8669e9479fa5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war" /><summary type="html">Iran on Friday offered the United States a seven-day plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz to maritime navigation. Initial word of a possible offer to lift the naval blockade emerged from the sidelines of the UN General Assembly earlier in the day. Read our liveblog to see how the day’s events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi reports fresh Houthi attacks as France pledges to defend key oil port</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7894f99557bfb1e895b3353a3489578dfb50de178edd0764989460da10af5eda</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:34:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-saudi-houthi-attacks-france-oil-port--b181320ddfb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-saudi-houthi-attacks-france-oil-port" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia intercepted Houthi ballistic missiles on Thursday after warning several regions, including Mecca, of possible attacks. France said it would send military assets to help protect the Saudi oil terminal at Yanbu. The strikes came amid renewed fighting in Yemen that has killed dozens, according to sources cited by AFP.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli PM Netanyahu calls Gaza genocide allegations ‘biggest lie of the century’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3adec96a7bc60848dc433e25cc8dc619434d6130d116d1fecea4ec78a9d2ca1c</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:31:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un--515acad11225.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gave a combative speech at the UN General Assembly on Thursday in which he denied that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza, lashed out at leaders, including New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani, and said attacking Iran was "one of the easiest decisions" he had ever made.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Residents in West Bank's Masafer Yatta face Israeli demolitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa8d5a2d3364e7ceb34a94487dd9451c909705600146302512aa853c3cf122e8</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:47:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions--70cf9dfea7fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions" /><summary type="html">On September 2, the Israeli army demolished the village of Khirbet a-Taban in the occupied West Bank. The village is located in Masafer Yatta, an area Israel declared a restricted military zone. Residents of the area have been reporting an increase in demolitions by the Israeli army and harassment by Israeli settlers since the October 7 Hamas attack.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: Trump will 'declare victory and go home', embracing the 'Greenland option'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84f9d33e9c52733e4168e41b4be672d5b5f3f01a5419c2832f6da80a833afb3a</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T02:35:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260924-us-war-on-iran-trump-will-declare-victory-and-go-home-embracing-the-greenland-option--6a5dcb3c91e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260924-us-war-on-iran-trump-will-declare-victory-and-go-home-embracing-the-greenland-option" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Scott Anderson, journalist, war correspondent and best-selling author of "King of Kings: The Fall of the Shah and the Revolution That Forged Modern Iran". For Anderson, there is a striking parallel between 1979 and 2026: Washington's persistent misreading of Iran, and the consequences that follow.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey to hand over military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f4925459e0b3ae810cd2c19d8d16e5f35a9bb936927f3549bd76bdf8c0a993b</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T00:02:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-turkey-to-hand-over-military-base-in-northern-iraq-to-baghdad--46f25e037ab4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-turkey-to-hand-over-military-base-in-northern-iraq-to-baghdad" /><summary type="html">Turkey will gradually hand over control of its Bashiqa military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad, Ankara and Baghdad said Wednesday, in a move aimed at strengthening Iraqi state authority and easing a long-running source of tension between the neighbours.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a985a3991bdc1d51cb359f9b17795f9f592be0df0272a5766e1c8fa2dc55c05</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:49:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address--10f22d78db02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01bf8aec8e53034808878769d919ba86f2c15a69ac12103e7a47a40208ae8e5a</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9bd4c94da86cf57582bb441ad4399a2bfdee8dfc9e5bdecb33fdd898ba1ff120</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1--ba655932baa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".</summary></entry><entry><title>Golan Heights will 'remain Syrian', President Ahmed al-Sharaa vows at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:159c6d7563bfc9e7de98caac1fa5b399e31c4f57620e7812071bdfe935c5f718</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:31:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un--f84fe9f69d85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un" /><summary type="html">Syria's President Ahmed al-Sharaa told the UN Wednesday that the contested Golan Heights region would "remain Syrian" despite ongoing military occupation by Israel. The Syrian leader also used his second turn at the UN rostrum to denounce repeated Israeli strikes on his country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UN General Assembly enters second day with key speeches ahead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26ee80455f75222307c9a99df797b2b5982e59931dd070bbbb3e1a24f49670d0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:10:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead--5f17c5aa8caa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead" /><summary type="html">It’s Day Two of the United Nations General Assembly in New York, with a packed programme including speeches by Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Some of the biggest names in artificial intelligence will also address the UN Security Council. France 24’s Jessica Le Masurier is covering the gathering for us.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel denounces Macron's UN remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d874c95c90ff12c56089c42a7d2abb8bde86d355da2dff2082ece837ae43dfe</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:56:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks--1be41b7349b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks" /><summary type="html">Israeli officials have hit back at French President Emmanuel Macron after he criticised Israel’s conduct in the occupied West Bank during his address to the UN General Assembly. But while Macron used strong words against Israel, France allowed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s plane to fly through French airspace on its way to New York, despite an ICC arrest warrant against him. Delano D’Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US President warns Tehran at UN but says talks ongoing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24b93c2c37cd9d24a520c29b52b8debaf5e9a0a27603248b4646eef03f855cdb</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:46:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing--e226200bdb56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing" /><summary type="html">The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel blasts ‘grotesque absurdity’ of Macron’s UN remarks on West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3f044de4c4990211a249afa99e5b759a334a85ef59851776f074de9118fbecf</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:41:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-israel-blasts-grotesque-absurdity-of-macron-s-un-remarks-on-west-bank--342a531dbd98.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-israel-blasts-grotesque-absurdity-of-macron-s-un-remarks-on-west-bank" /><summary type="html">The Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office on Wednesday issued a stinging rebuke to French President Emmanuel Macron's UN speech denouncing settler violence against Palestinians in the West Bank. Macron's remarks that "Hamas has never struck in the West Bank" was a "grotesque absurdity", said the statement.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US President Trump threatens "annihilation" of Iran despite successful talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d8116d101c0cff4e3694a387f25e05a4748ef10150b557f3f9950955a428dd2</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:22:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks--ffdddb023d23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks" /><summary type="html">The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. First, Morgan Ayre reports on the latest developments in the Middle East.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI risks, Iran war dominate agenda at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be76897262af1f62e9ef4bf2911f7c2fed21f36e98ac581ad2d6eb84bb94b0b8</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T05:29:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-ai-risks-iran-war-to-take-center-stage-at-un--4b4adc4994fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-ai-risks-iran-war-to-take-center-stage-at-un" /><summary type="html">France convenes a UN Security Council meeting Wednesday on artificial intelligence (AI) and international security, which includes briefings by leading industry figures, including the heads of OpenAI and Anthropic. The meeting comes as world leaders jostle over how to address the risks of the new technology. On the second day of the UN General Assembly, the Iran war is also set to dominate the agenda.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec13504392946b26db035a7bc9c10ecaf63399135097a19ae5ff74f986d99423</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T16:17:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms--aa11d208ea3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says envoys Witkoff, Kushner met with mediators on potential Iran deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cf6e2c65ae1c1df11565498676db19f6a29dfa184a6122ee16467400fa540b5</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T03:41:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un--4465411a8b3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday said ‌special envoys ‌Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner had met ‌with mediators on a possible deal to end the US war against Iran. Trump earlier threatened to "annihilate the Islamic Republic" if Tehran didn’t reach a peace deal with Washington in his UN General Assembly speech. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia left without US help against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:153399040d995023ce27968dabf777fca53f263ac7ba4d61e210966ee95428bd</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:57:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis--69e955589d82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia is weighing Washington’s refusal to help fend off Houthi attacks after Riyadh requested US assistance, despite the two countries being longstanding allies and President Donald Trump and his family maintaining close personal ties with Saudi leaders. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details on this alliance.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two tankers hit by 'unknown projectile' or debris in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9727416e6555d50bd72bd95dfa5a7654fb036f71e57099455d304b895660daba</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:03:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260921-projectile-hits-tanker-as-it-enters-the-strait-of-hormuz--07400cdd3c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260921-projectile-hits-tanker-as-it-enters-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz on Monday by either an "unknown projectile" or debris, a maritime security agency said. United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations added that at least two crew members were injured in the first incident, and both vessels will continue to their next port of call.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Israeli settler, Palestinian killed in latest violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:877b9f465dd55ed63bb0d07854b5535f3761a6b29ed22898b4e5fa6c01b50701</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:58:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settler-palestinian-killed-in-latest-violence--ac92b7366cc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settler-palestinian-killed-in-latest-violence" /><summary type="html">Violence flared in the Israeli-occupied West Bank on Sunday, as Israeli forces arrested a suspected Palestinian gunman accused of killing an Israeli man. In a separate incident, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian driver who the military said had attempted to run them over. Nicholas Rushworth reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli settler and Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09df011bd7cd05edb2321a0bccbf38d5b2521df921554abc28b6581dde9ec1ac</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T15:30:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--6ec13ca89571.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">A suspected Palestinian gunman on Sunday shot dead an Israeli man near a West Bank settlement, according to Israeli officials. The gunman was located at a Ramallah hospital and arrested, police said. Elsewhere in the West Bank, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian motorist who the military said was attempting to run them over. The flare up in violence came on the eve of the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
